Goal
* Please *either* remove the example entirely, as it simply repeats the Example section, *or* add some explanation to the example.

Input
* Please remove the last line ("Read s… spaces").

Cases
* Please swap the order of the two [[x]] strings in the following cases:

  • Separate matches (Validator 1)

  • Spaces inside search strings (Validator 5)

* Spaces inside search strings (Test 5 & Validator 5)

  • For one of the [[x]] strings, please use multiple spaces (e.g. "blue   dog") instead of a single space.

  • For [[s]], please include occurrences of each [[x]] in two forms: one with a single space, one with multiple spaces. (You could also add more forms.)

* Please add one test/validator pair for each of the following scenario:

  • Adjacent occurrences of different [[x]] strings, e.g. [[s]] = CodinGameCodinGameCodinGame, [[x1]] = Game, [[x2]] = Codin

  • A pair similar to "No match at minimum length" (Pair 4), but using a longer [[s]], longer [[x]] strings, and a larger [[n]].

  • A comprehensive pair, where:

    - every [[x]] string appears multiple times in [[s]];

    - the order of the first occurrences in [[s]] differs from the order of the [[x]] strings in the input;

    - some occurrences in [[s]] are adjacent for the same [[x]];

    - some occurrences are adjacent for different [[x]] strings;

    - some occurrences are separated by other text;

    - [[s]] also contains case-variant versions of some [[x]] strings;

    - length([[s]]) around 100;

    - shortest [[x]] length around 15;

    - longest [[x]] length around 50.

    - if necessary, reduce the length of [[s]] and [[x]] in the current final pair of cases, and use longer [[s]] and [[x]] strings in this new pair instead (i.e. increase the target lengths beyond 100 and 50).

Thanks.
